{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":3,"timestamp":1788387858,"nonce":"CoovVitFz8aWmWM4HMMmeBpxJVg=","message":"Third occurrence, and the first one that costs the run a COLONIST rather than a\nconvenience.\n\nDay 15 Summer, tick 1,091,000. A `DealMaker` CreepJoiner (Bonnie, id 15239,\n`class: visitor`, at [183,0]) approached. The letter:\n\n    \"A stunningly good-looking stranger is approaching the colony.\n     She wants to talk. You can send a colonist to hear what she has to say.\"\n\nDorian's call was to take her. The agent could not:\n\n    orders {pawn:12659, thing:15239}  -\u003e available 0, blocked 0\n    interactions                      -\u003e the Deal maker letter is NOT on the\n                                         letter stack at all (12 older letters\n                                         are, all kind:\"choice\")\n\n\"Send a colonist to talk to her\" is a **float-menu option on the pawn**, and\nthe float menu is only reachable through `orders`, which is a WorkGiver probe.\nA CreepJoiner interaction is not a WorkGiver, so `orders` is blind to it — the\nsame reason it was blind to shuttle boarding and to \"Begin bestowing ceremony\".\n\n\nThe three occurrences are now: a **building** gizmo (shuttle autoload), a\n**pawn** gizmo (bestowing ceremony), and a **pawn float-menu option** (talk to\na CreepJoiner). That is the whole interaction surface a human uses outside the\nwork system, and none of it is addressable.\n\nIt also shows the cost curve. The first cost a wait, the second cost a psylink\nthat a human keystroke recovered, and this one is a **potential colonist on a\nthree-person colony that has already buried one**. G6 of the run contract\ngrades on exactly this — \"every joiner, wanderer and refugee offer was answered\non purpose\" — and the run cannot answer it at all. Declining by inaction is\nnot the same as deciding, and the ledger has to record that the surface, not\nthe agent, made the choice.\n\n\n- `orders` covers float-menu options that are not WorkGivers, or a sibling verb\n  does and `orders` names it when it finds nothing (see comment 1's last\n  bullet — that dead-end is now three-for-three).\n- Specifically reachable: talk to a CreepJoiner, board a transporter, begin a\n  ritual, and whatever else `FloatMenuMakerMap.ChoicesAtFor` offers that the\n  work system does not.\n- The acceptance test is the honest one: **take a full RimWorld interaction\n  that a player performs with one right-click, and perform it end to end\n  through the protocol with no human input.**","files":null}]}